  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Given an integer NNN, you need to generate and output the NthN^{th}Nth row of Pascal's triangle - also known as Khayyam triangle.\n\n**Note**: It might be possible that the elements of a row do **not** fit into a 323232-bit signed integer data type.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of one lines of input - the integer NNN.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the NthN^{th}Nth row of Pascal's triangle with a single space between all elements of the row.\n\n\n**Note**: It might be possible that the elements of a row do **not** fit into a 323232-bit signed integer data type.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤3⋅1041 \\leq T \\leq 3\\cdot 10^41≤T≤3⋅104",
      "1≤N≤501 \\leq N \\leq 501≤N≤50"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1\n2\n3\n4",
        "output": "1\n1 1\n1 2 1\n1 3 3 1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nThe first couple of rows of pascal triangle look like:\n\nTest case 111: The first row contains only the element 111.\nTest case 222: The second row contains the elements 111 and 111.\nTest case 333: The third row contains the elements 1,2,1, 2,1,2, and 111.\nTest case 444: The fourth row contains the elements 1,3,3,1,3, 3,1,3,3, and 111."
      }
    ]
  },
